  "workflow_capture": {
    "summary": "Photopea exposes no public stream of semantic UI commands. To get a JSON of 'what happened' you either (A) use the built-in Actions recorder and convert its .ATN export, (B) drive/observe an embedded Photopea through Live Messaging with an injected recorder, or (C) capture browser-level input + document-state snapshots.",
    "methods": [
      {
        "id": "A",
        "name": "Actions panel recording (built-in, semantic)",
        "how": "Window > Actions. New Action Set, New Action, Record, perform the workflow, stop recording, then Export the set as an .ATN file.",
        "output": ".ATN (Adobe action format, binary) — one action set, ordered Steps. Parse to JSON.",
        "pros": ["No code injection", "Semantic operation names", "Replayable in Photopea itself"],
        "cons": ["Not every interaction is recorded (freehand strokes and some tool gestures are not action-able)", "Binary format needs a parser", "Steps are Photopea/Photoshop operation names, not low-level edits"]
      },
      {
        "id": "B",
        "name": "Live Messaging OE harness (scriptable)",
        "how": "Embed Photopea in your own page (iframe, https://www.photopea.com/#{...}), send a recorder script with iframe.contentWindow.postMessage(script, '*'), and receive events with app.echoToOE(JSON.stringify(evt)).",
        "output": "JSON lines, one per captured event.",
        "pros": ["You control both ends", "Can hook the public API, DOM key/mouse events and poll document state in one place", "Same channel Photopea plugins use"],
        "cons": ["Only public-API calls and DOM events are observable; the internal UI emits no public command event", "Requires you to host the harness page"]
      },
      {
        "id": "C",
        "name": "Browser input capture + state diffing",
        "how": "In the Photopea tab, record keydown/click and read menu labels to reconstruct commands from the keybind map above; snapshot app.activeDocument (layers, names, selection presence, size) on a timer and diff.",
        "output": "JSON event log with before/after state.",
        "pros": ["Captures everything the user actually pressed", "Works without the app exposing hooks"],
        "cons": ["Input-level, not semantic", "Measuring 'what changed' needs diffing heuristics"]
      }
    ],
    "recommended": "A for a replayable, semantic list of menu operations; B (with a small API/DOM recorder) when you need a continuous JSON log of a live session; combine A+B when you want both."
